# Thank You Girl, verse, second phrase: Paul's counterpoint over John (figure 16.4)
# John's lower line is the melody both sang in unison in the first phrase; Paul's line above it
# makes the "jumble of fourths and fifths" with a few sixths. Notes share each bar equally (the
# first note of each bar is typed with space after it, but no rhythm is marked).
#? Register: John's melody is placed A4-D5 with Paul above; it may lie an octave lower.
key D

system
voice "Paul"   | F#5 D5 E5 G5 | F#5 D5 E5 G5 | F#5 D5 C#5 B4 | A4 |
voice "John"   | A4 A4 B4 D5 | A4 A4 B4 D5 | A4 F#4 E4 D4 | D4 |
